# the corpse's spear: level by the near hand (the sword's drop holds its grip at about 5,-9 from the pivot). (P2c slice i3) three
# rows higher (origin 26 13): it lies on the ground behind the corpse, along its top edge, not across the body
# (INTEGRATE i2) the compositor lays the pivot items down after the turn (SLICE-DOLL i2), so this drop is SLICE-ARMS i2's
# upright drawing transposed (as the west turn would have laid it; the light stays top-left), level under the corpse
view L key drop origin 26 -1 anchor pivot layer heldBack
mark tip 0 2
|....v..................................
|..vvyv.................................
|vzyyywNiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiih
|..vxxvNhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhf
|....v..................................
regions
|.......................................
|.......................................
|.....NG................................
|...NN.R................................
|.......................................

# the carry at rest: upright in the right fist (`rest`; the run's `when run` is one row shorter). (P2c slice i3) Facing
# down, up and right the carry is on layer held, beside the body and over the near arm, so the haft runs unbroken from the
# fist to the leaf (i2's layer neck hid it behind the arm and the helm and left the leaf floating above the helm); facing
# left the fist is the far one, so the haft stays behind the head (layer neck) and shows over the torso. The loco arms
# mark handR, not grip, so the compositor draws no fist over the haft: each carry view draws the fist itself (skin steps,
# region H, so gloves and gauntlets recolour it) on the grip rows.
view D key rest origin 2 27 layer held
mark tip 2 0
